ADVANCE DOCKER COMMANDS CHEAT SHEET

🔴BASIC COMMANDS

→ docker --version = Show Docker version
→ docker info = Show system-wide information
→ docker help = Get help on Docker commands
→ docker = Show Docker CLI usage

🔵CONTAINERS MANAGEMENT

→ docker run image = Run a container
→ docker run -d image = Run in detached mode
→ docker run -it image = Run interactively with terminal
→ docker start container_id = Start stopped container
→ docker stop container_id = Stop running container
→ docker restart container_id = Restart container
→ docker pause container_id = Pause container
→ docker unpause container_id = Unpause container
→ docker rm container_id = Remove container
→ docker exec -it container_id bash = Open bash in container
→ docker exec -it container_id sh = Run shell inside container

🟤INSPECTING & VIEWING

→ docker ps = List running containers
→ docker ps -a = List all containers
→ docker logs container_id = View logs
→ docker inspect container_id = Inspect configuration
→ docker stats = Live resource usage
→ docker top container_id = Running processes

🟠IMAGES MANAGEMENT

→ docker images = List images
→ docker pull image = Download image
→ docker build -t tag . = Build image from Dockerfile
→ docker tag image new_tag = Tag image
→ docker rmi image = Remove image
→ docker image prune = Remove dangling images
→ docker system prune = Remove unused data

🟣VOLUMES & NETWORKS

→ docker volume ls = List volumes
→ docker volume create = Create volume
→ docker volume rm volume_id = Remove volume
→ docker network ls = List networks
→ docker network create = Create network
→ docker network connect network container_id = Connect container
→ docker network disconnect network container_id = Disconnect container

⚫CLEANING UP

→ docker system prune = Remove unused containers, images, networks
→ docker volume prune = Remove unused volumes
→ docker container prune = Remove stopped containers
→ docker image prune = Remove dangling images
→ docker network prune = Remove unused networks

🟢OTHER USEFUL COMMANDS

→ docker-compose up = Start services from compose file
→ docker-compose down = Stop and remove services
→ docker commit container_id new_image = Create image from container
→ docker save image > file.tar = Save image
→ docker load < file.tar = Load image
→ docker login = Login to registry
→ docker logout = Logout from registry
